    "result_text": "All 11 test classes ran and passed. The implementation is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Behavior:** When a create request has the same lastName+address (compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace) as an existing owner:\n- Without `sharesHousehold: true` \u2192 rejected 409 (existing behavior, unchanged).\n- With `sharesHousehold: true` \u2192 allowed, and both the new owner and the matched existing owner(s) are stamped with the same `householdId` \u2014 a stable identifier deterministically derived from the canonical lastName+address, so every owner joining that household gets the identical value. `householdId` is returned in the owner representation.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added read-only `householdId` to the `Owner` response schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persistent `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 ignore `householdId` when mapping the request fields DTO (it's pipeline-assigned; MapStruct maps it automatically on the response side).\n- `function/owner/EnsureUniqueHousehold.java` \u2014 now, on a match with sharing opted in, derives the shared id, stamps/saves the matching existing owner(s), and publishes it via `Out<HouseholdId>`; still throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` when sharing is not requested.\n- `function/owner/HouseholdId.java` (new) \u2014 a dedicated variable type so OfficeFloor's by-type matching stays unambiguous.\n- `function/owner/AssignHousehold.java` (new) \u2014 stamps the shared id onto the newly built owner.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired a `household-assign` step after `build`, within the same transaction.\n\n**Tests:** Full suite green \u2014 21 tests, 0 failures (including the new `Cp11Tests` shared-household check and the existing `Cp10Tests` duplicate/allow cases).",
